! The Spice Quarter Compitale

''Stratum:'' the sea-level ring, the market district · ''Scale:'' Site (one wedge room).
//(Seated from the Referee Noosphere Guide's worked session — the book's exemplar stands as
live geography.)//

A wedge-shaped room pressed between a textile merchant and a tea-seller, entered from the
crossroads by a low archway. Above the lintel: a carved orichalcum figure, small and worn, one
arm raised, holding a shallow dish — the rim recently smeared with cardamom oil.

''The walls:'' blood-red plaster floor to ceiling, decades of frescoes layered over older
frescoes — two serpents approaching a central altar from opposite sides, never quite meeting; a
peacock on the south wall, tail spread into the corner (one scorch mark, "decided decorative");
something dog-headed on the east wall (observed to reposition when unwatched); painted eggs in
painted greenery along the north shelf. The style runs illusionistic — in good light the eye
loses where the wall begins. A third serpent in the south fresco repositions between visits.

''The furnishings:'' the north offering shelf (brass incense burners in three sizes, figs and
pine nuts, a dried flower, a hole-drilled coin, a clay figure) · a small pinax to Eris Discordia
that dusts itself · three curtained hardware alcoves with Noosphere rigs of varying age · two
low cushion-tables · one long slept-on couch · MUG-SMOKE's counter at the back (chai hot, coffee
hotter, foam omens read on request) · the Realm portal — a standing orichalcum-inlaid archway,
warm to the touch, breathing slowly.

''The air:'' cinnamon, cardamom, old copper, faint ozone from the east road. Affinity: Fire,
Spice (+). District dressing nearby: the Weavers' District, the Glassblowers' Quarter, the
Undermarket behind the Cistern Wall, the East Gate warehouses.

